comments[2]:
  - created_at: "2026-11-07T10:00:00.820Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Root cause located (2026-11-07, while fixing a Codex review finding on the pm-gh1665/1666/1667 batch): wrapProgramActionsForExtensionHandlers in src/cli/main.ts wraps every Commander action and calls runActiveCommandHandler for a registered extension handler BEFORE the dynamic command action runs. validateDynamicExtensionCommandOptions lives only in that dynamic action (runRequiredExtensionCommand), so for a handler-backed command it is never reached. A command with declared flags is still guarded because extractCommandScopedOptions validates loose options against its definitions; a command with no flags is not. The batch PR closes only the root-only subset (--all/--explain) for every extension command, via refuseUndeclaredRootOnlyOptions in the wrapper. The general fix (call the zero-flag option validator in the wrapper) is deliberately left here: it can break packages whose handlers read options they never declared through registerFlags, so it needs a fleet census of package commands that read context.options without declarations, and a migration note.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-11-07T17:18:32.616Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Re-scoped after a fleet census (2026-11-07). Wiring a zero-flag refusal into the handler dispatch path works on the built CLI (pm demo-plain --bogus exits 2 unknown_option), but a read-only census of all 47 unbraind pm-* repos plus the bundled packages found 12 released zero-flag commands in 8 repos (example-only pm-cli-companion excluded) that read options they never declare, and pm-graph parses its flags from context.args (12 of 17 commands). Shipping the refusal now would break those packages for every user, so the handler path keeps passing undeclared options through and the refusal stays here.\n\nDelivered in this batch: child pm-1du7s3 (refusal on commands with declared flags carries code unknown_option and lists only declared plus inherited host flags; the dynamic-path zero-flag refusal gets the same code and list). Prerequisite before the flip: child pm-kl1nio (the package-side migration, with the census table). Once pm-kl1nio lands, wire refuseUndeclaredExtensionCommandOptions into wrapProgramActionsForExtensionHandlers in src/cli/main.ts (it is one call; the census run showed the exact refusal text) and meet AC 1, 2 and 4 here. Options considered and rejected: a stderr warning per invocation (noisy for every pm-graph user who cannot fix the package), and a per-command strict opt-in (new SDK surface that leaves the default lenient forever)."
    edited_at: "2026-11-07T17:18:51.777Z"
body: ""
